<title>USA: Carbo Ceramics Q4 pro forma shr $0.28.</title>
<headline>Carbo Ceramics Q4 pro forma shr $0.28.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended   Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>			     December 31,	   December 31,</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Revenues     $16,820,526 $13,809,834 $65,150,741 $58,000,940</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>  taxes (a)     6,337,921   4,764,667  22,682,635  21,713,257</p>
<p> Net income     4,053,674   4,764,667  16,800,040  21,713,257</p>
<p>Pro forma net</p>
<p>  income (b)    4,053,674   3,047,436  14,290,060  13,679,352</p>
<p>Pro forma average</p>
<p>shares outstanding (c)</p>
<p>		   14,735,333  14,602,000  14,693,803  14,602,000</p>
<p>Pro forma net</p>
<p>  income per share    .28	   .21	   .97	   .94</p>
<p>(a) Pretax income for the twelve months ended December 31, 1996 includes an incremental charge of $877,225 relating to the accelerated recognition of compensation expense for the vesting of restricted stock in connection with the Company's initial public offering.</p>
<p>(b) Pro forma net income based on the Company's effective tax rate. Prior to April 24, 1996 the Company and its shareholders had elected S Corporation status under the Internal Revenue Code.</p>
<p>(c) Represents the number of shares outstanding following the completion of the initial public offering of the Company's stock on April 26, 1996.  Weighted average number of shares for 1996 also reflects the issuance of stock options at the time of the initial public offering. SOURCE  Carbo Ceramics Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
